    "body":  "# CA Skill Compiler v2.1.0\n\n**Release source:** `b67fbb56c34d15b8d5a0903c8a7ca93d608f8f65`\n**Language target:** `connectionagent.io/v1alpha5`.\n\n- Adds independent Development v1alpha1 `BuildDevelopment` / `VerifyDevelopment`, CLI `build-development` / `verify-development`, and native + Go/WASM Worker support.\n- Validates exact immutable Interface Package snapshots, Dependency Lock closure, package-scoped Schema and Capability members; emits static Capability requirements and disjoint Host Admission / Runtime Execution requirement files.\n- Ships five reviewed Development v1alpha1 machine contracts; the release tag establishes their product contract baseline.\n- Development Artifact status remains LINKED / BUILT / NOT_ADMITTED. Production Host MUST reject DEVELOPMENT; no Owner, Deployment Grant, Runtime or 5GC qualification is claimed.\n- Keeps frozen v1alpha5 Build/Verify artifact bytes identical to v2.0.2. Its embedded generator.version=v2.0.2 denotes the frozen artifact generator contract (not the installed product version); new Development manifests stamp v2.1.0.\n- One Go Core with full Go tests, vet, CLI E2E, v2.0.2 golden regression, Development negative tests and real Chromium Worker artifact/diagnostic parity.\n\n**Assets:** Four native binaries, standalone Go/WASM, browser-ready Worker bundle (skillc.wasm, wasm_exec.js, skillc-worker.js), five-JSON-Schema Development contract archive, and SHA256SUMS.\n\n**Boundary:** Formal MAS author-source offline tests #53 remain separate and nonblocking. Owner/Provider/Host/Runtime/5GC admission and qualification are external.\n\n**History:** v2.0.2, v2.0.1, v2.0.0 and v1.0.0 Release assets and tags remain unchanged.\n"
